1gja|n|A piece of ground inclosed, and stored with beasts of the chase, which a man may have by prescription, or the king's grant. ; A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like. ; A piece of ground, in or near a city or town, inclosed and kept for ornament and recreation; as, Hyde Park in London; Central Park in New York. ; A space occupied by the animals, wagons, pontoons, and materials of all kinds, as ammunition, ordnance stores, hospital stores, provisions, etc., when brought together; also, the objects themselves; as, a park of wagons; a park of artillery. ; A partially inclosed basin in which oysters are grown.	a:1wav,80,1;1mo0,41,2~1mo0,41,2;1wav,80,1	n:64h,94,4;1wav,80,1;dsh,47,2~64h,94,4;dsh,47,2;1wav,80,1	N:1khh,31,2~1khh,31,2
