1gtf|n|A trodden way; a footway. ; A way, course, or track, in which anything moves or has moved; route; passage; an established way; as, the path of a meteor, of a caravan, of a storm, of a pestilence. Also used figuratively, of a course of life or action.	a:nie,89,3;6oz,78,2;fa9,53,6;1qr3,50,5;277y,46,5;2dc,46,4;zt6,32,3;1y6n,31,6;n4u,31,4;24k1,28,6~rpw,27,24;7c0,7,9;mu8,19,6;tu5,15,6;1y6n,31,6;d3y,9,6;fa9,53,6;24k1,28,6;1uus,9,5;2di,27,5	v:raw,37,4;chi,16,1;15kd,4,4~raw,37,4;15kd,4,4;chi,16,1	V:92r,34,3;1jbr,18,1~92r,34,3;1jbr,18,1	n:19ki,70,8;asx,39,46;1b56,34,4;raw,27,2;qp1,24,7;22p9,23,5;23e9,18,3;chi,16,1;sd9,13,2;n2a,12,4~asx,39,46;19ki,70,8;qp1,24,7;22p9,23,5;n2a,12,4;1b56,34,4;23e9,18,3;raw,27,2;rqc,4,2;sd9,13,2	N:1jbr,42,5;92r,28,2;ugz,25,1;t15,24,5;22xr,12,4;29i1,2,2~t15,24,5;1jbr,42,5;22xr,12,4;29i1,2,2;92r,28,2;ugz,25,1
