1gu9|n|The state or quality of being patient; the power of suffering with fortitude; uncomplaining endurance of evils or wrongs, as toil, pain, poverty, insult, oppression, calamity, etc. ; The act or power of calmly or contentedly waiting for something due or hoped for; forbearance. ; Constancy in labor or application; perseverance. ; Sufferance; permission. ; A kind of dock (Rumex Patientia), less common in America than in Europe; monk's rhubarb. ; Solitaire.	a:16i4,40,5;1b5y,24,6;1w1v,24,14;1awf,5,4~1w1v,24,14;1b5y,24,6;16i4,40,5;1awf,5,4	v:16vu,70,5;16vz,68,2;15k9,43,3;1z7h,41,3~16vu,70,5;1z7h,41,3;15k9,43,3;16vz,68,2	n:1krd,50,4~1krd,50,4
